  "_readme": "Framework-agnostic assembly description for DDScope Core. Declares which src/, fragments/, and styles/ files exist and the order each group loads in to reconstruct the page. This is the single source of truth for assembly order across all frameworks (see docs/DDScope_Modular_Architecture.md). 'order' values are historical CommWise SCRIPT/DIV/STYLE numbers, kept as-is for continuity and because their gaps already leave room for future insertions without renumbering — they no longer come FROM CommWise, they just happen to match it. frameworks/local/build.js reads this file directly. frameworks/commwise/sync-tracker.md keeps only CommWise-specific bookkeeping (block address, push date) and is not a source of order for any framework. Optional per-entry 'frameworks' array (e.g. ['framework-2']) scopes an entry to specific frameworks — absent means all frameworks (backward compatible default). frameworks/local/build.js includes an entry only if 'frameworks' is absent or contains 'framework-2'; frameworks/commwise/plan-push.js and record-push.js include an entry as a push candidate only if 'frameworks' is absent or contains 'framework-1'. See docs/DDScope_Assemblies.md §1 - Module block model.",

